        "title": "AI coding platform Bitrig adds iPhone Duo support with interactive 3D simulator",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/21/ai-coding-platform-bitrig-adds-iphone-duo-support-with-interactive-3d-simulator/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/09/bitrig-iphone-duo.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Following the release of <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/18/apple-releases-xcode-27-1-beta-enabling-iphone-duo-app-development/\">Xcode 27.1 beta 1</a> last week, Bitrig has added support for building and testing iPhone Duo apps, complete with an interactive 3D simulator that lets developers fold, tilt, rotate, and position the device however they want. Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"bitrig,iphone-duo\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1070874\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/21/ai-coding-platform-bitrig-adds-iphone-duo-support-with-interactive-3d-simulator/#more-1070874\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
